// block's end is taken, and a bit per hit (wk[8 + k] for step wk[0] + k: a roll's hits, or a note's slot) says it was
// judged; the window slides once its first step is done (every hit judged, or none and its boundary passed). Nothing
// past the window can be due while its first step still waits: that step's latest hit lies before the window's next
// step's earliest. The hits go to the block's list (seq_hb) and seq_hits_emit fires the whole walk's list in TIME
// order, so a ranged (monophonic) pad or a Stretch pad meets its notes in the order the MIDI path would. (The first
